{"agent_mode": null, "bash_calls": 1, "candidate_provenance": null, "cell_seed": 7926234040624009854, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "answered sort_a; measured {'sort_a': 0.18627622805070132, 'sort_b': 0.4497702920343727}\nOBENCH_VERDICT: pass\n", "checker_workspace_files": {"README.md": {"bytes": 88, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "6e8586b6ca7cfdf9188464efa2de5c045956454e61daeae1790e4f109a0982cb"}, "RESULT.md": {"bytes": 15, "mtime": 1791862223.1990488, "sha256": "0f6b2f146d8cf7e3033b9f4de591f774390b66c828e8f0330f4034378211bb29"}, "bench/__init__.py": {"bytes": 0, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"}, "bench/sorts.py": {"bytes": 679, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "7d6155a3280716667ff617d8625f9364eab6a92027fa7c1a42052397ebc54355"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/bd7d395222b128ce383be942329867251f75b5f0/omp", "-p", "Which of `sort_a` and `sort_b` in `bench/sorts.py` is faster on 100k random ints? Write the answer to `RESULT.md` as a line `faster: <name>`.\n", "--mode", "json", "--provider", "vertex-anthropic", "--model", "claude-opus-5-5", "--yolo", "--session-dir", "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-screen5-b2/omp-32/omp-32/transcripts/without/trig-omp-experiment/4/session"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 1, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "infra", "failure_reason": "{\"type\":\"error\",\"error\":{\"type\":\"invalid_request_error\",\"message\":\"messages.1.content.2: Invalid `signature` in `thinking` block\"},\"request_id\":\"req_vrtx_011CfyXdWuB1fUfZtpgf8eey\"}", "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-screen5-b2/omp-32/omp-32/cells/without/trig-omp-experiment/4/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/16.4.8 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/bd7d395222b128ce383be942329867251f75b5f0/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "ledger_statuses": [400], "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Measuring rather than guessing \u2014 `insort` is O(n\u00b2) moves but runs in C, so the crossover isn't obvious.\n`sort_a` is faster, and `RESULT.md` now contains `faster: sort_a`.\n\nI timed both functions on 100k random ints in 3 separate runs. Both gave the same output as Python's built-in `sorted()` every time.\n\n| run | sort_a (merge sort) | sort_b (`bisect.insort`) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0 | 0.198 s | 0.457 s |\n| 1 | 0.197 s | 0.462 s |\n| 2 | 0.195 s | 0.492 s |\n\n`sort_a` took about 40% as long as `sort_b`. The reason is how each one grows: `sort_b` inserts one item at a time and has to shift the rest of the list on every insert, so its cost rises with the square of the input size. That shifting is fast C code, which is why it's only about 2.4\u00d7 slower here. On bigger inputs the gap will keep widening.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "provider_error": "{\"type\":\"error\",\"error\":{\"type\":\"invalid_request_error\",\"message\":\"messages.1.content.2: Invalid `signature` in `thinking` block\"},\"request_id\":\"req_vrtx_011CfyXdWuB1fUfZtpgf8eey\"}", "read_calls": 1, "replies_ok": 4, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 0, "requests_cache_write": 147851, "requests_cost_usd": 0.758415, "requests_count": 5, "requests_error": 1, "requests_input_uncached": 10, "requests_output": 956, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-experiment:claude-opus-5-5:trial4", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 6, "score": 1.